  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "",
    "overview": "Hermes is a pocket guide to the campus day. It should feel collected, useful, and human: a page someone would keep in their bag, opened on a phone between classes. Cool mineral paper gives the interface daylight and breathing room. Amber suggests discovery and momentum; copper adds a richer editorial note. The reference is a well made city guide, not an illustration of the Greek god.\n\nThe product surfaces are **Operate**: students scan, filter, inspect, and decide quickly. The landing page is **Persuade**, with more expressive type and a guide cover composition. The same colors, type, and rules carry across both.\n",
